      "description": "Watch Lommel SK vs Charleroi highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 17, 2026. On August 17, 2026, Lommel SK hosted Sporting Charleroi in a closely contested Jupiler Pro League fixture. Both teams approached the match with a focus on tactical discipline, leading to a game where every inch of the pitch was fiercely contested. Tactical Battle and Half-Time Adjustments The opening 45 minutes were defined by a cagey atmosphere as both sides struggled to find a breakthrough. With the scores level at halftime, Lommel SK looked to seize the initiative by making a double substitution. Shawn Adewoye and Juho Talvitie were introduced for Henry Oware and Isaiah Dada-Mascoll , signaling a more attacking intent for the second period. Boukamir Finds the Breakthrough As the second half progressed, the momentum began to shift. Lommel SK continued to refresh their lineup, bringing on Sverre Halseth Nypan and Antoine Colassin just before the hour mark. However, it was Sporting Charleroi who ultimately broke the deadlock. In the 63rd minute, Amine Boukamir found the back of the net with a clinical finish, sending the away supporters into raptures. Lommel responded with a triple change in the 71st minute, introducing Isaac Cisse , Freddy Mbemba , and Noah Solheid to salvage the match. Tense Finale and Final Whistle The closing stages were marked by rising tension and a flurry of activity on the touchline. Lommel SK captain Lucas Schoofs received a yellow card in the 85th minute as the physical intensity reached its peak. Despite late tactical gambles involving Zalan Vancsa and Mohamed El Boukammiri , the home side could not break through the organized Sporting Charleroi defense. After four minutes of stoppage time, the referee blew the final whistle, confirming a hard-earned victory for the visitors."
